Thank you for the update! This example works now.
I tried to adapt this back into my actual simulation, but there is still a problem. Earlier I thought the problem was with activators, but it turns out it's caused by from().

I'm using your example from the github issue post because it's much shorter. For example, this works:

simulate2 <- function() {
  env <- simmer(mon=monitor_csv())
  env <- env %>%
    add_generator("dummy", trajectory(), function() {rnorm(1, 5, 2)}) %>%
    run(5) %>%
    wrap()
  env
}

for (i in 1:2000)
  env <- simulate2()

But this gives the error "Error in file(file, "rt") : unable to open connection":

simulate3 <- function() {
  env <- simmer(mon=monitor_csv())
  env <- env %>%
    add_generator("dummy", trajectory(), from(1,function() {rnorm(1, 5, 2)})) %>%
    run(5) %>%
    wrap()
  env
}

for (i in 1:2000)
  env <- simulate3()

Extracting the info and rm'ing the environment, as you showed in this post, also gives the same error.

Thanks!

